cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use featuretree in research or a product, please cite it."
type: software
title: "featuretree: round-trip editable feature trees from a neutral IR, for AI- and code-generated CAD"
authors:
  - family-names: Newcome
    given-names: Dan
repository-code: "https://github.com/punkfab/featuretree"
url: "https://github.com/punkfab/featuretree"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-06-26"
abstract: >-
  featuretree authors a CAD design once as a small neutral feature IR (named, ordered
  operations; edges selected by query, never by kernel id) and emits it as a native, editable
  parametric feature tree in FreeCAD and Onshape, and as a build123d solid, from one source.
  Human edits made in the CAD GUI read back by feature name, so they survive regeneration and
  flow back to the code. A STEP->IR recogniser recovers a parametric tree from a frozen B-rep
  (extrude/revolve in any orientation, multi-axis pockets and cross-axis holes) and
  self-verifies every recovery by re-emitting the tree and comparing volume and bounding box
  to the original, reporting VERIFIED or honestly PARTIAL rather than a silently wrong guess.
  It is the editable round-trip layer that code- and LLM-generated CAD otherwise lacks.
keywords:
  - CAD
  - parametric modeling
  - feature tree
  - feature recognition
  - round-trip editing
  - FreeCAD
  - Onshape
  - build123d
  - AI-generated CAD
  - topological naming
